5.0 Manufacturing Considerations
5.1 Assembly Process:
text
1.  Mold pulp/PLA shell halves (injection molding)
2.  Apply food-grade silicone liner (spray coating)
3.  Install baffle system (snap-fit assembly)
4.  Load dry powder matrix (automated filling)
5.  Fill liquid compartments (through fill ports)
6.  Pressurize with nitrogen (to 30 psi)
7.  Install central dispersal charge & fuze
8.  Seal nose cone (threaded/tamper-evident)
9.  Attach fins (snap-fit, biodegradable adhesive)
10. Quality check: X-ray for voids, weight, fuze test
5.2 Cost Estimate (High Volume):
Shell & structural: $120

Chemical payload: $280

Dispersal charge & fuze: $350

Assembly & testing: $150

Total Unit Cost: ~$900 (at 10,000 unit production)

